- op: discuss  # 0086
  at: '2026-07-02T17:13:41Z'  # 0086
  by: agent  # 0086
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0086
  clock: 3  # 0086
  nonce: '0086'  # 0086
  message: "SPLIT. Part A (MECHANICAL) LANDED — PR #387: urllib.request.urlretrieve added to io_boundary.HIGH_RISK_PRIMITIVES (is_high_risk('urllib.request.urlretrieve') is now True, was False; catalog python.yaml already had all three urllib fns as net_send). Part B (DECISION-GATED, needs human/ADR) REMAINS: the filed fix also asks to extend the high-risk COMPLETENESS RATCHET (test_io_boundary.py TestHighRiskPrimitivesDriftGuard, currently 'if p.boundary != subprocess: continue') from subprocess to net/fs. Unlike subprocess (clean invariant: subprocess == arbitrary exec == high risk), net/fs has NO clean high-risk invariant — stat/open are benign, urlopen/rmtree are not — so classifying the ~1400 currently-unclassified net_send/net_recv/fs_write/fs_read primitives across the 14 catalogs as high-risk-or-exempt requires an ADR on the net/fs risk taxonomy first, or the ratchet cascades false positives. Awaiting a human ruling on that taxonomy before Part B can be built."  # 0086
