  message: "Resolved via ruling 1b (dev c3a2f6df45). high_risk RETIRED as a net/fs risk axis: net/fs risk is carried by the taint source/sink model (AUTO_SINK_ZONE_MAP, ADR-0017 §2b) + supply-chain dst_tier — the considered, spec-documented taxonomy that high_risk was an undocumented display-only SHADOW of (0 hits in any ADR/spec/schema; 0 verify-claims/taint consumers). Part B ('extend the ratchet to net/fs') → NOT built, ratifying WI-sugav's deliberate 2026-05-28 non-decision (net/fs has no clean 'always risky' invariant; an exemption list would cascade FPs). Part A's urlretrieve addition REVERTED (net_send->network taint sink carries egress risk). Behavioral evidence: is_high_risk('urllib.request.urlretrieve')/('shutil.rmtree') now False (test_io_boundary.py); subprocess ratchet unchanged; smart-test green (4648 passed). Full provenance: decision_register_06102026.md UPDATE 2026-07-04."  # ae0f
